'''Veiled modifiers''' can be found on items, primarily those dropped by [[Immortal Syndicate]] members. The modifier will do nothing until it is unveiled by right-clicking the item. Unveiling the mod presents three random mods, and allows the player to choose which one the veiled mod becomes.

As long as an item has at least one veiled mod it will have [[File:Veiled-item-symbol.png]] symbol in front and at the back of its name; the item loses its status as a veiled item once all mods have been unveiled.

Most veiled modifiers are more powerful versions of [[Crafting Bench]] modifiers which also do not count as a crafted mod. Some unique veiled items have exclusive veiled modifiers.

== How to obtain ==
Veiled items primarily drop from [[Immortal Syndicate]] members during a Betrayal encounter.

Veiled items with two veiled mods can drop from Syndicate members if [[Secrets Unveiled]] is allocated or from Safehouses with [[Aisling Laffrey]] stationed in Transportation or Fortification.

Syndicate members can occasionally drop a {{il|Veiled Chaos Orb}}, which reforges a Rare item's mods like a regular Chaos Orb, but with one veiled mod. The [[Syndicate Mastermind]] can drop a {{il|Veiled Exalted Orb}}, which can be used on a Rare item to remove a random modifier then add a veiled mod.

[[Abyss jewel]]s can drop with a veiled modifier if [[Suffused with Darkness]] is allocated. This is the only source of veiled items outside of Betrayal encounters.

